<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Reuss-Greiz</h1><p class="st-meta">1564 CE – 1918 CE · capital Greiz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Elder Line of the house of Reuss, ruling from Greiz, one of the smallest states of the German Empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the division of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-reuss">Reuss</a> lands in 1564, the Elder Line received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greiz">Greiz</a> and the surrounding part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-plauen">Vogtland</a>. After a split into Upper and Lower Greiz, the branches were reunited in 1768, and in 1778 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-xi-prince-reuss-of-greiz">Heinrich XI</a> was raised to prince of the empire.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like their cousins, all male members were named Heinrich, but the Elder Line numbered them in a sequence that restarted at intervals. The principality was small, Lutheran and agrarian, later with textile mills in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greiz">Greiz</a> and Zeulenroda. Its upper and lower castles still dominate the town.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-reuss">Reuss</a> Elder Line sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1866 and was occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, but joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a> in 1871, and Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-xxii-prince-reuss-of-greiz">Heinrich XXII</a> remained a noted opponent of Prussian policy. After the revolution of 1918 it merged with the Younger Line in 1919 into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peoples-state-of-reuss">People's State of Reuss</a>, part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> from 1920.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-reuss-greiz.jpg" alt="Principality of Reuss-Greiz" width="320" height="255"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_F%C3%BCrstentum_Reu%C3%9F_%C3%A4ltere_Linie.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1564 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Greiz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Heinrich XI, Heinrich XXII</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Reuss Elder Line, Reuß älterer Linie</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1741&amp;focus=principality-of-reuss-greiz" aria-label="Principality of Reuss-Greiz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4958 419 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Reuss-Greiz lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5278 675L5229 694M5278 675L5199 691M5278 675L5300 622M5278 675L5275 669"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5199 691h0M5300 622h0M5275 669h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5278 675h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5278 675h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Greiz. <a href="/atlas?year=1741&amp;focus=principality-of-reuss-greiz">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
